"UFC on ESPN 72: How to watch Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Vegas lineup, odds, more","UFC on ESPN 72: How to watch Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Vegas lineup, odds, more (This story was updated to add new information.) The UFC stays in its “Sin City” home base for a second straight week with a big middleweight clash at the top of the bill. Here's how to watch UFC on ESPN 72 with 185-pound contenders in the headlining spot. Broadcast and streaming info UFC on ESPN 72 has a main card that airs at 9 p.m. ET on ESPN. The preliminary card airs on ESPN and streams on ESPN+ at 6 p.m. ET. Veteran broadcaster Dan Hellie serves as desk anchor and host at UFC on ESPN 72. Former UFC middleweight champion Chris Weidman, welterweight veteran Alan Jouban and coach Din Thomas join him at the desk as analysts throughout the broadcast and on the post-fight show. Longtime UFC correspondent and host Karyn Bryant will conduct pre and post-fight interviews backstage with some of the athletes on the UFC on ESPN 72 card, as well as report additional real-time updates for the event. John Gooden will serve as the leading man on the mic from cageside at UFC on ESPN 72. He'll command play-by-play and be joined in the booth by UFC Hall of Famer Daniel Cormier and former UFC/WEC champion Dominick Cruz. Din Thomas will also join the booth during the broadcast as a coach-analyst. (Mike Bohn–MMA Junkie) Main event: Roman Dolidze - Record: 15-3 MMA, 9-3 UFC - Opponent: Anthony Hernandez (14-2 MMA, 8-2 UFC) - Division: Middleweight - Key wins: Marvin Vettori, Kevin Holland, Anthony Smith, Jack Hermansson - Misc.: Dolidze had a stellar four-fight run a few years back that included three bonuses, but then he ran into a two-fight skid. That’s well in the rearview mirror, though. He’s now won three straight against former light heavyweight title challenger Anthony Smith, Kevin Holland and former middleweight title challenger Marvin Vettori – which avenged a decision loss from two years prior. Main event: Anthony Hernandez - Record: 14-2 MMA, 8-2 UFC - Opponent: Roman Dolidze (15-3 MMA, 9-3 UFC) - Division: Middleweight - Key wins: Brendan Allen, Michel Pereira, Roman Kopylov, Edmen Shahbazyan, Marc-Andre Barriault - Misc.: It’s been more than five years since Hernandez was stopped in just 39 seconds by Kevin Holland. Since then, he has seven straight wins – including five by stoppage and three post-fight bonuses. A win over Dolidze would make it hard to deny him the right to ask for a title shot. Co-main event: Steve Erceg - Record: 12-4 MMA, 3-3 UFC - Opponent: Ode Osbourne (13-8 MMA, 5-6 UFC) - Division: Bantamweight - Key wins: Matt Schnell - Misc.: Erceg got a title shot on the strength of a 3-0 start in the UFC, including two post-fight bonuses. But he dropped a decision to champ Alexandre Pantoja 15 months ago, which set off his current three-fight skid that includes losses to recent title challenger Kai Kara-France and former champ Brandon Moreno, the latter of which came in March. Erceg was set to fight Alex Perez, who pulled out. Then HyunSung Park was rebooked to fight Tatsuro Taira two days ago, making Osbourne Erceg’s third opponent. Due to the short notice, the fight will take place at bantamweight and not flyweight. Co-main event: Ode Osbourne - Record: 13-8 MMA, 5-6 UFC - Opponent: Steve Erceg (12-4 MMA, 3-3 UFC) - Division: Bantamweight - Key wins: Charles Johnson, CJ Vergara - Misc.: On the heels of a three-fight skid and four losses in five bouts, Osbourne got a crucial win in April when he took out Luis Gurule with a bonus-winning knockout. That was his first win in more than two years after losses to Asu Almabayev, Jafel Filho and Ronaldo Rodriguez. Due to the short notice, the fight will take place at bantamweight and not flyweight. UFC on ESPN 72 lineup MAIN CARD (ESPN, ESPN+, 7 p.m. ET) - Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez - Steve Erceg vs. Ode Osbourne - Angela Hill vs. Iasmin Lucindo - Andre Fili vs. Christian Rodriguez - Miles Johns vs. Jean Matsumoto - Eryk Anders vs. Christian Leroy Duncan PRELIMINARY CARD (ESPN, ESPN+, 4 p.m. ET) - Rafael Cerqueira vs. Julius Walker - Toshiomi Kazama vs. Elijah Smith - Priscila Cachoeira vs. Joselyne Edwards - Uros Medic vs. Gilbert Urbina - Gabriella Fernandes vs. Julija Stoliarenko - Cody Brundage vs. Eric McConico UFC on ESPN 72 main card betting odds - Dolidze +250, Hernandez -340 - Erceg -400, Osbourne +285 - Hill +150, Lucindo -190 - Fili +170, Rodriguez -225 - Johns +240, Matsumoto -330 - Anders +340, Leroy Duncan -500 UFC on ESPN 72 prelim betting odds - Cerqueira +400, Walker -620 - Kazama +390, Smith -590 - Cachoeira +215, Edwards -290 - Medic -390, Urbina +280 - Fernandes -440, Stoliarenko +310 - Brundage -200, McConico +150",2025-08-04,https://mmajunkie.usatoday.com/story/sports/ufc/2025/08/04/ufc-espn-72-roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-start-time-lineup-odds/85501445007/
"2025 UFC event schedule: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Dricus du Plessis vs. Khamzat Chimaev on tap","2025 UFC event schedule: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Dricus du Plessis vs. Khamzat Chimaev on tap Check out a complete list of UFC pay-per-view and Fight Night events scheduled for 2025 The UFC middleweight division takes center stage. Contender Anthony Hernandez and Roman Dolidze headline UFC Fight Night on Saturday, one week before UFC 319's blockbuster title fight between Dricus du Plessis and Khamzat Chimaev. Dolidze and Hernandez are running relatively hot hands. Dolidze is on a three-fight winning streak and hopes to reignite belief in a run to the top. ""Fluffy"" Hernandez has won seven straight, but only makes small incremental ranking gains due to UFC matchmaking. Another win for Hernandez sets him up, hopefully, for bigger names. Next week, UFC middleweight champion Du Plessis makes arguably his most anticipated title defense against Chimaev. Chimaev, long deemed a future champion, earned his shot by violently submitting Robert Whittaker. Du Plessis has exceeded everyone's expectations. His dominant run includes wins over Israel Adesanya, Sean Strickland (twice) and Whittaker. Du Plessis vs. Chimaev headlines UFC 319. A late addition co-main event pits UFC debutant Aaron Pico against featherweight contender Lerone Murphy. Take a look below at the current UFC event schedule for 2025. Be sure to check back on this page for more information on upcoming UFC events throughout the year. Upcoming UFC Schedule | Event | Date | Main event | Weight class | Location | TV | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | UFC Fight Night | Aug. 9 | Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez | Middleweight | Las Vegas | ESPN+ | | UFC 319 | Aug. 16 | Dricus du Plessis (c) vs. Khamzat Chimaev | Middleweight title | Chicago | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Aug. 23 | Johnny Walker vs. Zhang Mingyang | Light heavyweight | Shanghai | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Sept. 6 | Nassourdine Imavov vs. Caio Borralho | Middleweight | Paris | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Sept. 13 | Diego Lopes vs. Jean Silva | Featherweight | San Antonio, Texas | ESPN+ | | UFC FIght Night | Sept. 27 | Carlos Ulberg vs. Dominick Reyes | Light heavyweight | Perth, Australia | ESPN+ | | UFC 320 | Oct. 4 | Magomed Ankalaev vs. Alex Pereira 2 | Light heavyweight title | Las Vegas | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Oct. 11 | TBA | TBA | Rio de Janeiro | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Oct. 18 | TBA | TBA | Vancouver | ESPN+ | | UFC 321 | Oct. 25 | Tom Aspinall vs. Ciryl Gane | Heavyweight title | Abu Dhabi | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Nov. 22 | TBA | TBA | Doha, Qatar | ESPN+ |",2025-08-05,https://www.cbssports.com/mma/news/2025-ufc-event-schedule-roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-dricus-du-plessis-vs-khamzat-chimaev-on-tap/
UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results - Dolidze vs. Hernandez,"UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez Get the latest UFC Vegas 109 weigh-in results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez Las Vegas, NV – UFC is set to electrify the APEX once again on Saturday, August 9, with a high-stakes UFC Fight Night headlined by a clash of ranked middleweight contenders, No. 8 Roman Dolidze and No. 9 Anthony Hernandez. The action-packed night also features a critical flyweight co-main event as Alex Perez faces off against Steve Erceg. The official weigh-in results are available below. The event will be broadcast live on ESPN, ESPN Deportes, and ESPN+, with prelims kicking off at 3 p.m. PT / 6 p.m. ET and the main card beginning at 6 p.m. PT / 9 p.m. ET. MAIN EVENT: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez Roman Dolidze (15-3), hailing from Batumi, Georgia, makes his second UFC headlining appearance. With signature wins over Marvin Vettori, Kevin Holland, and Anthony Smith, Dolidze enters the bout aiming to solidify his place in the Top 5 of the middleweight division. Anthony “Fluffy” Hernandez (14-2, 1 NC), from Dunnigan, California, rides a dominant seven-fight winning streak, highlighted by finishes over Michel Pereira, Roman Kopylov, and Edmen Shahbazyan. A win over Dolidze would mark the biggest moment of his UFC career. CO-MAIN EVENT: Alex Perez vs. Steve Erceg Alex Perez (25-9), a Contender Series veteran and former title challenger, brings elite striking and wrestling to the Octagon. He looks to maintain momentum after victories over Matheus Nicolau, Jussier Formiga, and Jordan Espinosa. Steve Erceg (12-4) of Perth, Australia, aims to bounce back from a recent loss and reestablish his position in the flyweight title mix. Known for his finishing ability, Erceg holds wins over Matt Schnell, Alessandro Costa, and David Dvořák. How to Watch: - Network: ESPN, ESPN Deportes, ESPN+ - Prelims: 3 p.m. PT / 6 p.m. ET - Main Card: 6 p.m. PT / 9 p.m. ET - Location: UFC APEX, Las Vegas, Nevada UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez: Main Card (ESPN, ESPN+, 7 p.m. ET) - Roman Dolidze (185.5) vs. Anthony Hernandez (186.5)* - Steve Erceg (135.5) vs. Ode Osbourne (135.5) - Angela Hill (116) vs. Iasmin Lucindo (115) - Andre Fili (146) vs. Christian Rodriguez (146) - Miles Johns (136) vs. Jean Matsumoto (136) - Eryk Anders (186) vs. Christian Leroy Duncan (185) Prelims (ESPN, ESPN+, 4 p.m. ET) - Rafael Cerqueira (203) vs. Julius Walker (206) - Toshiomi Kazama (136) vs. Elijah Smith (136) - Priscila Cachoeira (134) vs. Joselyne Edwards (136.5)** - Uros Medic (171) vs. Gilbert Urbina (171) - Gabriella Fernandes (125.5) vs. Julija Stoliarenko (126.25)*** - Cody Brundage (202.5) vs. Eric McConico (204.5) - *Hernandez missed the middleweight limit by 0.5 pounds on the first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD - ** Edwards missed women’s bantamweight limit by 0.25 pounds on first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD - *** Stoliarenko missed the women’s flyweight limit by 0.25 pounds on the first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD Roberto Villa is the CEO, Founder, Executive Writer, Senior Editor of FightBook MMA. Has a passion for Combat Sports and also a podcast host for Sitting Ringside. He’s also a former MMA fighter and Kickboxer. Discover more from FightBook MMA Subscribe to get the latest posts sent to your email.",2025-08-08,https://www.fightbookmma.com/ufc-vegas-109-weigh-in-results-dolidze-vs-hernandez-updates/
