"2025 UFC event schedule: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Dricus du Plessis vs. Khamzat Chimaev on tap","2025 UFC event schedule: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez, Dricus du Plessis vs. Khamzat Chimaev on tap Check out a complete list of UFC pay-per-view and Fight Night events scheduled for 2025 The UFC middleweight division takes center stage. Contender Anthony Hernandez and Roman Dolidze headline UFC Fight Night on Saturday, one week before UFC 319's blockbuster title fight between Dricus du Plessis and Khamzat Chimaev. Dolidze and Hernandez are running relatively hot hands. Dolidze is on a three-fight winning streak and hopes to reignite belief in a run to the top. ""Fluffy"" Hernandez has won seven straight, but only makes small incremental ranking gains due to UFC matchmaking. Another win for Hernandez sets him up, hopefully, for bigger names. Next week, UFC middleweight champion Du Plessis makes arguably his most anticipated title defense against Chimaev. Chimaev, long deemed a future champion, earned his shot by violently submitting Robert Whittaker. Du Plessis has exceeded everyone's expectations. His dominant run includes wins over Israel Adesanya, Sean Strickland (twice) and Whittaker. Du Plessis vs. Chimaev headlines UFC 319. A late addition co-main event pits UFC debutant Aaron Pico against featherweight contender Lerone Murphy. Take a look below at the current UFC event schedule for 2025. Be sure to check back on this page for more information on upcoming UFC events throughout the year. Upcoming UFC Schedule | Event | Date | Main event | Weight class | Location | TV | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | UFC Fight Night | Aug. 9 | Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez | Middleweight | Las Vegas | ESPN+ | | UFC 319 | Aug. 16 | Dricus du Plessis (c) vs. Khamzat Chimaev | Middleweight title | Chicago | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Aug. 23 | Johnny Walker vs. Zhang Mingyang | Light heavyweight | Shanghai | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Sept. 6 | Nassourdine Imavov vs. Caio Borralho | Middleweight | Paris | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Sept. 13 | Diego Lopes vs. Jean Silva | Featherweight | San Antonio, Texas | ESPN+ | | UFC FIght Night | Sept. 27 | Carlos Ulberg vs. Dominick Reyes | Light heavyweight | Perth, Australia | ESPN+ | | UFC 320 | Oct. 4 | Magomed Ankalaev vs. Alex Pereira 2 | Light heavyweight title | Las Vegas | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Oct. 11 | TBA | TBA | Rio de Janeiro | ESPN+ | | UFC Fight Night | Oct. 18 | TBA | TBA | Vancouver | ESPN+ | | UFC 321 | Oct. 25 | Tom Aspinall vs. Ciryl Gane | Heavyweight title | Abu Dhabi | ESPN+ PPV | | UFC Fight Night | Nov. 22 | TBA | TBA | Doha, Qatar | ESPN+ |",2025-08-05,https://www.cbssports.com/mma/news/2025-ufc-event-schedule-roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-dricus-du-plessis-vs-khamzat-chimaev-on-tap/
UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results - Dolidze vs. Hernandez,"UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez Get the latest UFC Vegas 109 weigh-in results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez Las Vegas, NV – UFC is set to electrify the APEX once again on Saturday, August 9, with a high-stakes UFC Fight Night headlined by a clash of ranked middleweight contenders, No. 8 Roman Dolidze and No. 9 Anthony Hernandez. The action-packed night also features a critical flyweight co-main event as Alex Perez faces off against Steve Erceg. The official weigh-in results are available below. The event will be broadcast live on ESPN, ESPN Deportes, and ESPN+, with prelims kicking off at 3 p.m. PT / 6 p.m. ET and the main card beginning at 6 p.m. PT / 9 p.m. ET. MAIN EVENT: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez Roman Dolidze (15-3), hailing from Batumi, Georgia, makes his second UFC headlining appearance. With signature wins over Marvin Vettori, Kevin Holland, and Anthony Smith, Dolidze enters the bout aiming to solidify his place in the Top 5 of the middleweight division. Anthony “Fluffy” Hernandez (14-2, 1 NC), from Dunnigan, California, rides a dominant seven-fight winning streak, highlighted by finishes over Michel Pereira, Roman Kopylov, and Edmen Shahbazyan. A win over Dolidze would mark the biggest moment of his UFC career. CO-MAIN EVENT: Alex Perez vs. Steve Erceg Alex Perez (25-9), a Contender Series veteran and former title challenger, brings elite striking and wrestling to the Octagon. He looks to maintain momentum after victories over Matheus Nicolau, Jussier Formiga, and Jordan Espinosa. Steve Erceg (12-4) of Perth, Australia, aims to bounce back from a recent loss and reestablish his position in the flyweight title mix. Known for his finishing ability, Erceg holds wins over Matt Schnell, Alessandro Costa, and David Dvořák. How to Watch: - Network: ESPN, ESPN Deportes, ESPN+ - Prelims: 3 p.m. PT / 6 p.m. ET - Main Card: 6 p.m. PT / 9 p.m. ET - Location: UFC APEX, Las Vegas, Nevada UFC Vegas 109 Weigh-in Results – Dolidze vs. Hernandez: Main Card (ESPN, ESPN+, 7 p.m. ET) - Roman Dolidze (185.5) vs. Anthony Hernandez (186.5)* - Steve Erceg (135.5) vs. Ode Osbourne (135.5) - Angela Hill (116) vs. Iasmin Lucindo (115) - Andre Fili (146) vs. Christian Rodriguez (146) - Miles Johns (136) vs. Jean Matsumoto (136) - Eryk Anders (186) vs. Christian Leroy Duncan (185) Prelims (ESPN, ESPN+, 4 p.m. ET) - Rafael Cerqueira (203) vs. Julius Walker (206) - Toshiomi Kazama (136) vs. Elijah Smith (136) - Priscila Cachoeira (134) vs. Joselyne Edwards (136.5)** - Uros Medic (171) vs. Gilbert Urbina (171) - Gabriella Fernandes (125.5) vs. Julija Stoliarenko (126.25)*** - Cody Brundage (202.5) vs. Eric McConico (204.5) - *Hernandez missed the middleweight limit by 0.5 pounds on the first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD - ** Edwards missed women’s bantamweight limit by 0.25 pounds on first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD - *** Stoliarenko missed the women’s flyweight limit by 0.25 pounds on the first attempt; bout status and fine amount TBD Roberto Villa is the CEO, Founder, Executive Writer, Senior Editor of FightBook MMA. Has a passion for Combat Sports and also a podcast host for Sitting Ringside. He’s also a former MMA fighter and Kickboxer. Discover more from FightBook MMA Subscribe to get the latest posts sent to your email.",2025-08-08,https://www.fightbookmma.com/ufc-vegas-109-weigh-in-results-dolidze-vs-hernandez-updates/
UFC Vegas 109: Dolidze vs. Hernandez Weigh-In Results,"For the second straight week, the UFC octagon is back at the Apex in Las Vegas, with UFC Vegas 109 headlined by ranked middleweights Roman Dolidze and Anthony “Fluffy” Hernandez. Last weekend’s Apex affair had a downright dreadful lack of star power, but produced some very, very entertaining fights. Could this week’s outing offer similar value? Without question, UFC Vegas 109 boasted bigger names than its predecessor, with former title challenger Steve Erceg in action in the co-main event, and names like Eryk Anders, Andre Fili, and Angela Hill taking part. Weigh-ins for UFC Vegas 109 get underway on Friday, August 8, 2025 starting at 12PM ET, 9AM PT. Full results from Friday’s official weigh-in can be found below. UFC Vegas 109: Dolidze vs. Hernandez Weigh-In Results Main card Middleweight: Roman Dolidze (185.5) vs. Anthony Hernandez (186)* Bantamweight: Steve Erceg (135.5) vs. Ode’ Osbourne (135.5) Women’s Strawweight: Iasmin Lucindo (115) vs. Angela Hill (116) Featherweight: Andre Fili (146) vs. Christian Rodriguez (146) Bantamweight: Miles Johns (136) vs. Jean Matsumoto (136) Middleweight: Eryk Anders (186) vs. Christian Leroy Duncan (185) Preliminary card Light Heavyweight: Julius Walker (206) vs. Raffael Cerqueira (203) Bantamweight: Elijah Smith (136) vs. Toshiomi Kazama (136) Women’s Bantamweight: Joselyne Edwards (136.)** vs. Priscila Cachoeira (134) Welterweight: Uroš Medić (171) vs. Gilbert Urbina (171) Women’s Flyweight: Gabriella Fernandes (125.5) vs. Julija Stoliarenko (126.)*** Light Heavyweight: Cody Brundage (202.5) vs. Eric McConico (204.5) * Hernandez made weight on second attempt ** Edwards made weight on second attempt *** Stoliarenko made weigh ton second attempt",2025-08-08,https://cagesidepress.com/2025/08/08/ufc-vegas-109-dolidze-vs-hernandez-weigh-in-results/
"UFC Vegas 109 fight card, start time, date and location | Dolidze vs. Hernandez","Event: UFC Vegas 109: “Dolidze vs. Hernandez” Date: Sat., Aug. 9, 2025 Location: UFC APEX in Las Vegas, Nevada Broadcast: ESPN/ESPN+ Start Time: 4 p.m. ET Prelims Card | 7 p.m. ET Main Card UFC Vegas 109 fight card, start time, date and location | Dolidze vs. Hernandez It’s a battle of Top 10 middleweight contenders when Roman Dolidze collides with Anthony Hernandez atop the UFC Vegas 109 fight card this weekend at APEX, with the winner moving to the top of a very short list of eligible 185-pound title contenders! UFC Vegas 109 Main Event On ESPN/ESPN+: 185 lbs.: Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez UFC Vegas 109 Main Card on ESPN/ESPN+ (7 p.m. ET): 125 lbs.: Steve Erceg vs. Ode Osbourne 115 lbs.: Angela Hill vs. Iasmin Lucindo 145 lbs.: Andre Fili vs. Christian Rodriguez 145 lbs.: Miles Johns vs. Jean Matsumoto 185 lbs.: Eryk Anders vs. Christian Leroy Duncan UFC Vegas 109 Prelims Card on ESPN/ESPN+ (4 p.m. ET): 205 lbs.: Julius Walker vs. Raffael Cerqueira 135 lbs.: Elijah Smith vs. Toshiomi Kazama 135 lbs.: Priscila Cachoeira vs. Joselyne Edwards 170 lbs.: Uros Medic vs. Gilbert Urbina 125 lbs.: Gabriella Fernandes vs. Julija Stoliarenko 205 lbs.: Cody Brundage vs. Eric McConico *Fight card, bout order and amount of fights remain subject to change.* MIDDLEWEIGHT MAYHEM! Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) returns to its APEX facility in Las Vegas, Nevada, on Sat., Aug. 9, 2025, with UFC Vegas 109. That’s where No. 8-ranked Middleweight contender, Roman Dolidze, clashes with No. 10-seeded Anthony Hernandez in a high-stakes main event showdown scheduled for five, five-minute rounds. In UFC Vegas 109’s co-main event, former Flyweight title challenger, Steve Erceg, takes on Ode Osbourne, with both fighters looking to climb the 125-pound rankings. MMAmania.com will deliver LIVE round-by-round, blow-by-blow coverage of the entire UFC Vegas 109 fight card RIGHT HERE, starting with the ESPN+ “Prelims” undercard bouts at 4 p.m. ET, followed by the remaining main card balance on ESPN/ESPN+ at 7 p.m. ET. To checkout the latest and greatest UFC Vegas 109 news and notes be sure to hit up our comprehensive event archive here.",2025-07-04,https://www.mmamania.com/2025/7/4/24461707/ufc-vegas-109-fight-card-start-time-date-location-dolidze-vs-hernandez-apex-espn-mma
Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Preview & Picks – Fluffy To Earn Points Win At UFC APEX,"How to Watch UFC Fight Night: Dolidze vs Hernandez Live Stream 29 Jul 2025 Read More Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Preview & Picks – Fluffy To Earn Points Win At UFC APEX - Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez picks for Saturday, August 9 - UFC Fight Night is taking place at the UFC APEX in Las Vegas, Nevada - Preview, predictions, stats & form - Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Preview & Picks - Roman Dolidze Form - Anthony Hernandez Form Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Preview & Picks Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Preview & Picks Anthony Hernandez is tipped to score a decision victory over Roman Dolidze. Hernandez is a cardio machine with great wrestling, so we expect him to grapple, smother and frustrate Dolidze for five rounds. - Anthony Hernandez is on a 7-fight win streak - All 3 of Roman Dolidze’s career defeats have been by decision - 4 of Roman Dolidze’s last 5 fights have gone the distance Roman Dolidze Form Roman Dolidze is the number eight ranked middleweight contender with a professional record of 15-3 (8 KOs, 3 Subs). Dolidze made his UFC debut in 2020 and made a successful start in the light-heavyweight division, knocking out Khadis Ibragimov and out-pointing John Allan. He moved down to middleweight after that and endured a rough debut as he dropped a decision to Trevin Giles. The 37-year-old Georgian recovered quickly with a points win over Laureano Staropoli, and backed that up by knocking out Kyle Daukaus, Phil Hawes and Jack Hermansson in 2022. Dolidze’s rise was halted by a points loss to Marvin Vettori, and he then dropped a decision to Nassourdine Imavov. He has not lost since though, sparking a three-fight win streak with a decision victory over Anthony Smith. Dolidze then ended 2024 with a first-round knockout of Kevin Holland, before beginning his 2025 campaign with a points win over Marvin Vettori. Anthony Hernandez Form Anthony Hernandez is the number nine ranked middleweight contender with a career record of 14-2 (3 KOs, 8 Subs) with 1 No Contest. Hernandez joined the UFC in 2019 but got off to a rough start as he lost two of his first three fights. He rallied though, and kick-started a seven-fight win streak with a second-round submission win over Rodolfo Vieira. The 31-year-old Californian then backed that up with a decision win over Josh Fremd, before submitting Marc-Andre Barriault in the third round. Hernandez kept the stoppage wins coming in his sole outing of 2023, knocking out Edmen Shahbazyan in the third round, and he stayed on a roll in 2024 too. ‘Fluffy’ began the year with a second-round stoppage win over Roman Kopylov, before knocking out Michel Pereira in the fifth and final round. He then opened 2025 with a unanimous decision win over Brendan Allen back in February. Verdict Anthony Hernandez has found the blueprint to success – cardio wrestling. He has done a great job of wearing out his opponents over the past few years, but Dolidze is a hard man to stop so the judges may be required. He has done a great job of wearing out his opponents over the past few years, but Dolidze is a hard man to stop so the judges may be required. 55 Stake Cash no deposit & 550,000 Gold Coins & 5% Rakeback Use promo code NEWBONUS Sign up with the code NEWBONUS. When you verify your account get 25 Stake Cash for free PLUS 250,000 Gold Coins and 5% Rakeback! No deposit required. Login each day for the next 30 days and get an additional 30 Stake Cash AND 300,000 Gold Coins. 21+ only. T&Cs apply. Excludes WA, NY, NV, ID, KY, MI, VT, NJ, DE, WV, PA, RI & MD. 55 Stake Cash no deposit & 550,000 Gold Coins & 5% Rakeback Use promo code NEWBONUS Sign up with the code NEWBONUS. When you verify your account get 25 Stake Cash for free PLUS 250,000 Gold Coins and 5% Rakeback! No deposit required. Login each day for the next 30 days and get an additional 30 Stake Cash AND 300,000 Gold Coins. 21+ only. T&Cs apply. Ex