"Top 10 UFC middleweights Roman Dolidze, Anthony Hernandez headline Aug. 9 Fight Night","Top 10 UFC middleweights Roman Dolidze, Anthony Hernandez headline Aug. 9 Fight Night A key middleweight bout is headlining a UFC Fight Night event in August. Promotionally ranked top 10 middleweights Roman Dolidze and Anthony Hernandez will headline a UFC Fight Night on Aug. 9 at UFC Apex in Las Vegas. MMA Junkie confirmed the booking with with two sources following a first report from X user @realkevink. Dolidze (15-3 MMA, 9-3 UFC) enters his third UFC main event while on a three-fight winning streak. After his last setback against Nassourdine Imavov, the Georgian won a unanimous decision over Anthony Smith, won by TKO against Kevin Holland, and most recently outpointed Marvin Vettori in a March main event to avenge a prior loss. In the latest USA TODAY Sports/MMA Junkie middleweight rankings, Dolidze holds the No. 11 spot with Hernandez (14-2 MMA, 8-2 UFC) one spot ahead at No. 10. ""Fluffy"" will become a UFC headliner for the second time. Currently riding a seven-fight winning streak, Hernandez has been steadily climbing the ladder, and is now knocking on the door of the division's elite. In his first main event opportunity at UFC Fight Night 245, Hernandez ground and pounded Michel Pereira for a fifth-round stoppage. He followed that up with a unanimous decision over Brendan Allen in his first fight of 2025. Current Aug. 9 UFC Fight Night lineup - Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez - Eryk Anders vs. Chris Duncan - Angela Hill vs. Iasmin Lucindo - Rafael Cerqueira vs. Julius Walker - Gabriella Fernandes vs. Julija Stoliarenko",2025-05-26,https://mmajunkie.usatoday.com/story/sports/ufc/2025/05/26/ufc-vegas-109-roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-middleweight-main-event/83822496007/
"UFC Fight Night Saturday fight card, main event time, live stream: How to watch Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez?","While fans continue to speculate on how many more wins he’ll need to earn a shot at gold, Hernandez remains unfazed. Focused and confident, he anticipates an action-packed fight, calling Dolidze (15-3 MMA, 9-3 UFC) the ideal opponent to help deliver a thrilling main event. Both fighters are on a roll, and Saturday’s clash could be pivotal in shaping the 185-pound title picture. With Dricus Du Plessis and Khamzat Chimaev currently leading the middleweight contender rankings, a dominant win from either Hernandez or Dolidze could vault them into the conversation for a future high-stakes showdown. HOW TO WATCH DOLIDZE VS HERNANDEZ FIGHT IN LAS VEGAS - Date: August 9, Saturday - Start Time: 7PM ET (Main Card) - Start Time: 4PM ET (Preliminary Card) - Venue: UFC APEX in Las Vegas, Nevada - Channel/Streaming: ESPN/ESPN+ MAIN CARD MATCHES: - Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez (Middleweight) - Steve Erceg vs Ode’ Osbourne (Bantamweight) - Iasmin Lucindo vs Angela Hill (Women’s Strawweight) - Andre Fili vs Christian Rodriguez (Featherweight) - Miles Johns vs Jean Matsumoto (Bantamweight) - Eryk Anders vs Christian Leroy Duncan (Middleweight) PRELIMINARY CARD MATCHES: - Julius Walker vs Rafael Cerquiera (Light Heavyweight) - Elijah Smith vs Toshiomi Kazama (Bantamweight) - Joselyne Edwards vs Priscila Cachoeira (Women’s Bantamweight) - Uros Medic vs Gilbert Urbina (Welterweight) - Gabriella Fernandes vs Julija Stoliarenko (Women’s Flyweight) (Catch all the US News, UK News, Canada News, International Breaking News Events, and Latest News Updates on The Economic Times.) Download The Economic Times News App to get Daily International News Updates. (Catch all the US News, UK News, Canada News, International Breaking News Events, and Latest News Updates on The Economic Times.) Download The Economic Times News App to get Daily International News Updates.",2025-08-06,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/us/ufc-fight-night-saturday-fight-card-main-event-time-live-stream-how-to-watch-roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez/articleshow/123138285.cms
UFC Vegas 109 staff picks including Anthony Hernandez to conquer Roman Dolidze and more predictions,"UFC Vegas 109 is the last stop on the road to UFC 319, and the Bloody Elbow experts have given their view on who will walk out the winner. In a card chock-full of interesting fights, it is the main event featuring Anthony Hernandez and Roman Dolidze that is drawing the fans’ attention in the build-up. Both men are top 10-ranked Middleweights with an eye on a future title fight, with very little to separate them so far in their careers. Elsewhere, a Women’s Strawweight clash is also expected to impress, as Iasmin Lucindo and Angela Hill face off in a packed main card. The Bloody Elbow staff has made their predictions about what will happen at UFC Vegas 109, including the two main event fights as well as the Fight of the Night and Performance of the Night bonus winners - READ MORE – Anthony Hernandez earned the nickname ‘Fluffy’ as a 15-year-old which confused one UFC legend Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez predictions - Ross Markey: Anthony Hernandez - Kyle Dimond: Anthony Hernandez - Hamish Woodward: Anthony Hernandez The Bloody Elbow experts are completely in agreement on the winner of the UFC Vegas 109 main event. Hernandez is the clear favorite, with Ross, Kyle, and Hamish all backing “Fluffy” to beat the #9-ranked fighter on Saturday. Despite being ranked below Dolidze, Hernandez boasts a seven-fight win streak since 2021, and should have the finishing ability to end the Georgian before time runs out in Las Vegas. While Dolidze has his own win streak going, years after his own suspension before even making his debut, which includes wins over Marvin Vettori and Kevin Holland, he is not expected to rise in the ranking after losing to Hernandez on August 9. Iasmin Lucindo vs Angela Hill predictions - Ross Markey: Iasmin Lucindo - Kyle Dimond: Iasmin Lucindo - Hamish Woodward: Iasmin Lucindo Once again, the staff picks are all in agreement with the winner of this fight. All three experts have chosen the #8-ranked Lucindo to continue her ascent up the Women’s Strawweight division by beating Hill in their co-main event fight. Recent victories over Marina Rodriguez and Karolina Kowalkiewicz have catapulted her into the top ten, and she seems unlikely to lose to Hill, after she lost to Amanda Lemos at UFC 313. Lucindo is a veteran in the division but could be pushing for one last reign at the top with a victory at UFC Vegas 109, which all the experts predict will happen. UFC Vegas 109 Fight of the Night - Ross Markey: Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez - Kyle Dimond: Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez - Hamish Woodward: Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez The main event of UFC Vegas 109 is, unsurprisingly, the fight that the experts are most looking forward to at the event. The bout features two men who can end a fight at any time, with five of Hernandez’s last seven fights (all victories) ending via submission or knockout. Eleven of Dolidze’s fifteen bouts in his career have had definitive finishes, although he will struggle to put away such an impressive striker as Hernandez without a bit of luck. No other fights seem to come close to the hype around Dolidze vs Hernandez, which looks more and more likely to earn the $50,000 Fight of the Night bonus. UFC Vegas 109 Performance of the Night - Ross Markey: Steve Erceg - Kyle Dimond: Christian Rodriguez - Hamish Woodward: Anthony Hernandez There is finally some disagreement as the experts have three different choices for who will earn the Performance of the Night bonus at UFC Vegas 109. Ross is backing Steve Erceg, finally on the card after a host of cancellations, to use his ample prep time to put on an impressive performance to earn himself that cash bonus. Erceg was supposed to face Tatsuro Taira at the event following another Alex Perez withdrawal, before the Japanese fighter moved up to the main event UFC Vegas 108, while his replacement Ode’ Osbourne doesn’t look up to the Erceg challenge a week later. Meanwhile, Christian Rodriguez is Kyle’s pick to impress, five months after his decision defeat against Melquizael Costa. Rodriguez has had a mixed record in the last two years, but he has put on some impressive wins when he has been victorious, and Andre Fili looks likely to be his next victim. Finally, Hamish once again cannot look past Hernandez, who is expected to put on a fantastic performance to sweep all the awards at UFC Vegas 109.",2025-08-07,https://bloodyelbow.com/2025/08/07/ufc-vegas-109-staff-picks-including-anthony-hernandez-to-conquer-roman-dolidze-and-more-predictions/
Anthony Hernandez vs Roman Dolidze Prediction and Picks – August 9,"Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Picks and Prediction – 8/9/2025 Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Prediction The UFC Apex in Las Vegas hosts a middleweight main event on August 9, 2025, featuring Roman Dolidze (+240) against Anthony Hernandez (-280) in a five-round clash at UFC Vegas 109. This matchup pits two well-rounded fighters with contrasting styles, promising an intriguing battle. Here's a preview of the fight, including fighter backgrounds, key factors, and betting insights. Roman Dolidze (13-3, 8 finishes) Hailing from Georgia, Dolidze is a versatile fighter known for his grappling prowess and improving striking. With a 7-3 UFC record, his notable wins include Jack Hermansson and Marvin Vettori. Dolidze’s grappling is his cornerstone, with four submission victories in the UFC, leveraging his judo and Brazilian jiu-jitsu black belt. His striking has evolved, showing crisp boxing and powerful kicks, though he can be vulnerable to high-volume strikers. Posts on X highlight Dolidze’s underrated grappling and ability to match Hernandez’s pace, with some bettors eyeing value in his +270 odds. However, his recent 1-2 record in his last three fights raises questions about consistency against top-tier competition. Anthony Hernandez (12-2, 9 finishes) The American, Hernandez, enters as the betting favorite, riding a five-fight win streak, including victories over Rodolfo Vieira and Marc-André Barriault. Known for his relentless pace and elite grappling, Hernandez averages 5.8 submission attempts per 15 minutes, among the highest in the division. His striking is functional but less polished, relying on volume and pressure to set up his ground game. X posts suggest Hernandez could dominate, with some calling it a “levels” performance, citing his superior cardio and grappling edge. Yet, his tendency to absorb strikes could be exploited by Dolidze’s power. Fight Breakdown This fight hinges on grappling exchanges and pace. Dolidze’s judo throws and submission skills could challenge Hernandez, especially early, but Hernandez’s cardio and relentless pressure may wear Dolidze down in later rounds. On the feet, Dolidze’s cleaner striking contrasts with Hernandez’s volume, making takedown defense critical for the Georgian. The Apex’s smaller cage favors grapplers, likely benefiting Hernandez’s chain-wrestling style. Betting markets lean toward Hernandez, but Dolidze’s upset potential lies in landing a heavy shot or securing a submission. Betting Insight For those looking to wager, Hernandez’s -280 odds reflect his momentum, but Dolidze at +240 offers value for risk-takers. Prop bets like Hernandez by submission (+150) or the fight going over 2.5 rounds (-110) are worth considering, given both fighters’ durability. For expert analysis and free betting tips, check out UFC picks for detailed predictions. Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez Pick Analysis Hernandez’s pace and grappling likely overwhelm Dolidze in the later rounds, leading to a decision or late submission. However, Dolidze’s power and grappling make him a live underdog. Expect a competitive war with Hernandez edging out a victory. Our Free MMA Pick for Anthony Hernandez vs Roman Dolidze Anthony Hernandez -280",2025-07-08,https://freepicks.picksandparlays.net/more-free-picks/mma-picks/roman-dolidze-at-anthony-hernandez-picks-and-predictions-8-9-25
UFC on ESPN: Dolidze vs. Hernandez - Wikipedia,"UFC on ESPN: Dolidze vs. Hernandez | UFC on ESPN: Dolidze vs. Hernandez | |||| |---|---|---|---|---| | Promotion | Ultimate Fighting Championship | ||| | Date | August 9, 2025 | ||| | Venue | UFC Apex | ||| | City | Enterprise, Nevada, United States | ||| | Event chronology | |||| | UFC on ESPN: Dolidze vs. Hernandez (also known as UFC on ESPN 72 and UFC Vegas 109) is an upcoming mixed martial arts event produced by the Ultimate Fighting Championship that will take place on August 9, 2025, at the UFC Apex in Enterprise, Nevada, part of the Las Vegas Valley, United States.[1] Background [edit]A middleweight bout between Roman Dolidze and former LFA Middleweight Champion Anthony Hernandez is scheduled to headline this event.[1] They were initially scheduled to compete at UFC 302 in June 2024 but Hernandez was forced out of the bout due to a torn ligament in his hand.[2] A women's bantamweight bout between former UFC Women's Bantamweight Championship challenger Mayra Bueno Silva and Joselyne Edwards was expected to take place at this event.[3] However, Bueno Silva pulled out due to undisclosed reasons and was replaced by Priscila Cachoeira.[4] Former UFC Flyweight Championship challengers Alex Perez and Steve Erceg were scheduled to meet in the co-main event.[5] However, Perez pulled out in mid-July due to undisclosed reasons and was replaced by Road to UFC Season 1 flyweight winner Park Hyun-sung.[6][7] In turn, Park was moved to UFC on ESPN: Taira vs. Park one week prior to compete in the main event after the original opponent Amir Albazi had to withdraw due to injury and was replaced by Ode' Osbourne in a bantamweight bout.[8][9] Fight card [edit]| Main card (ESPN / ESPN+) | ||||||| |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---| | Weight class | Method | Round | Time | Notes | ||| | Middleweight | Roman Dolidze | vs. | Anthony Hernandez | |||| | Bantamweight | Steve Erceg | vs. | Ode' Osbourne | |||| | Women's Strawweight | Iasmin Lucindo | vs. | Angela Hill | |||| | Featherweight | Andre Fili | vs. | Christian Rodriguez | |||| | Bantamweight | Miles Johns | vs. | Jean Matsumoto | |||| | Middleweight | Eryk Anders | vs. | Christian Leroy Duncan | |||| | Preliminary card (ESPN / ESPN+) | ||||||| | Light Heavyweight | Julius Walker | vs. | Raffael Cerqueira | |||| | Bantamweight | Elijah Smith | vs. | Toshiomi Kazama | |||| | Women's Bantamweight | Joselyne Edwards | vs. | Priscila Cachoeira | |||| | Welterweight | Uroš Medić | vs. | Gilbert Urbina | |||| | Women's Flyweight | Gabriella Fernandes | vs. | Julija Stoliarenko | |||| | Light Heavyweight | Cody Brundage | vs. | Eric McConico | See also [edit]References [edit]- ^ a b Marina Magomedova (2025-05-08). ""Dolidze vs. Hernandez to headline UFC event on August 9"". telecomasia.net. Retrieved 2025-05-15. - ^ Jed Meshew (2024-04-29). ""Anthony Hernandez out of UFC 302 fight with Roman Dolidze"". mmafighting.com. Retrieved 2025-05-18. - ^ Diego Ribas (2025-06-01). ""UFC encaminha Mayra Sheetara vs Joselyne Edwards para agosto, em Las Vegas"". agfight.com. Retrieved 2025-06-01. (in Brazilian Portuguese) - ^ Jean-Paul Francis Botello (2024-07-14). ""Joselyne Edwards confirma su próximo pleito con Priscila Cachoeira"". laestrella.com.pa. Retrieved 2025-07-16. (in Spanish) - ^ Mitchell Woodcock (2025-06-02). ""Former UFC flyweight title contender Steve Erceg concedes another loss could cost him his contract"". thewest.com.au. Retrieved 2025-06-02. - ^ Garrett Kerman (2025-07-17). ""Alex Perez out, Steve Erceg awaits a new challenger at UFC Vegas 109"". sports.yahoo.com. Retrieved 2025-07-17. - ^ Kyle Dimond (2025-07-19). ""Former UFC title challenger receives replacement undefeated opponent after coming closest to dethrone dominant champ"". bloodyelbow.com. Retrieved 2025-07-19. - ^ Sportsnet Staff (2025-07-28). ""Taira gets new UFC Fight Night main event opponent with Albazi out"". sportsnet.ca. Retrieved 2025-07-28. - ^ Garrett Kerman (2025-07-29). ""Steve Erceg gets third opponent in Ode Osbourne at UFC Vegas 109"". clutchpoints.com. Retrieved 2025-07-29. - ^ ""UFC on ESPN: Dolidze vs. Hernandez"". Ultimate Fighting Championship. Retrieved 2025-06-04.",2025-05-27,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UFC_on_ESPN:_Dolidze_vs._Hernandez
